infographic compare-binary-horizontal-underline-text-vs
data
  title IPC names the bottleneck the flame graph hides
  desc Same wide leaf on the flame graph — the IPC counter decides which fix actually works
  compares
    - label Memory-stalled
      children
        - label Memory-stalled — IPC < 1.0
          desc High cache-miss rate; the CPU is stalled waiting on cache or RAM (~100 ns per L3 miss), not retiring instructions
        - label Fix: data layout
          desc Struct-of-arrays, cache-friendly traversal, prefetching, smaller structs
        - label Algorithm rewrite won't help
          desc A faster but still memory-bound parser stalls just the same
    - label Compute-bound
      children
        - label Compute-bound — IPC > 2.5
          desc Low cache-miss rate; the CPU retires useful instructions every cycle, so the algorithm is the limit
        - label Fix: vectorisation / SIMD
          desc Smarter math or a better algorithm cuts the real work being done
        - label Data-layout fixes won't help
          desc Memory access isn't the bottleneck — prefetch and SOA buy nothing here
theme
  palette #6366f1 #14b8a6
